language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Calvin puzzle: fill an n by n grid with the numbers 1 to n*n, each once, so that consecutive numbers are placed by the movement rules.
given n : int(1..)
$ the allowed moves between two squares, with each square numbered (row-1)*n+column
letting MovesC = [ [(r1-1)*n+c1, (r2-1)*n+c2] | r1 : int(1..n), c1 : int(1..n), r2 : int(1..n), c2 : int(1..n), ((|r1 - r2| = 3) /\ (c1 = c2)) \/ ((r1 = r2) /\ (|c1 - c2| = 3)) \/ ((|r1 - r2| = 2) /\ (|c1 - c2| = 2)) ]
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n*n)
find rowOf : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n)
find colOf : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n)
find cell : matrix indexed by [int(1..n*n)] of int(1..n*n)
branching on [cell]
such that
$ every number from 1 to n*n is placed in exactly one square
allDiff(flatten(x)),
allDiff(cell),
$ each square holds the number that rowOf and colOf give for it
forAll k : int(1..n*n) . ((cell[k] = (rowOf[k] - 1) * n + colOf[k]) /\ (x[rowOf[k], colOf[k]] = k)),
$ the next number is placed vertically or horizontally exactly three squares away (a two square gap)
$ or diagonally exactly two squares away (a one square gap)
forAll k : int(1..n*n-1) . table([cell[k], cell[k+1]], MovesC)
